Sira: (Me and Jitendra head back to the long house earlier than usual after completing our daily tasks.)
Sira: (I lay down on my bed with a sigh and stare at the wooden ceiling.)
Sira: (Today's events fills my mind like a pesut circling around.)
Sira: (From the moment when the sun barely peeked over the horizon while I sneaked into the Sacred Forest.)
Sira: (When my father found me and scolded me for hours.)
Sira: (When I couldn't stand the stares coming from everyone before the Manajah Antang ceremony started and I left to be somewhere alone.)
Sira: (When Jitendra encouraged me to talk to everyone, and-)
Sira: (They didn't really hate me.)
Sira: (Except, maybe, my father's usual cold demeanor.)
Sira: (But after talking to each of them, I realised that perhaps I was a bit too harsh to myself.)
Sira: (I was too harsh to this village.)
Sira: (My dad, Balian Bawi, my friends, and even the wild animals that accidentally became part of our family.)
Sira: (A warm feeling filled my chest to the brim like it was going to pour out from the glass.)
Sira: (One day, I'm going to explore the outside world and learn what's out there.)
Sira: (Or maybe even find a new place to stay so I can be independent.)
Sira: (But for now.)
Sira: (This is my home.)
Jitendra: What are you smiling like an idiot for?
Sira: Thinking of how to make you fall from the tree again for being nosy.
Jitendra: Ouch, I don't have enough legs left to break. Have some mercy,[pause=1] please?
*Sira tilts her head to the side and looks at Jitendra in the dim sunset light*
*a soft expression spreads over his face like a blanket upon meeting her gaze*
Sira: Shut up. I'm trying to sleep.
Jitendra: Sira.
Sira: What?
Jitendra: ...
Jitendra: Nevermind.
Jitendra: Let's go to sleep, yeah? There's a lot we need to do tomorrow.
Sira: Alright.
Sira: *yawns*
*Sira turns her back on him and falls asleep almost immediately*
*the rest of the village pours into the house one by one to end their day*
